Template: hawser/mode
Type: select
Choices: standard, edge
Default: standard
Description: Connection mode:
 Standard mode listens for connections from Dockhand.
 Edge mode connects outbound to Dockhand over WebSocket and does not
 require inbound access to this host.
 .
 These settings are saved in /etc/hawser/config on installation. To change
 them later, edit that file and restart Hawser.

Template: hawser/bind_address
Type: string
Description: Listening address:
 IP address on which Hawser should accept connections.
 .
 Leave this empty to listen on all addresses.

Template: hawser/port
Type: string
Default: 2376
Description: Listening TCP port:
 TCP port on which Hawser should accept connections.

Template: hawser/invalid_port
Type: error
Description: Invalid port
 The port must be a number between 1 and 65535.

Template: hawser/token
Type: password
Description: Authentication token:
 Token clients must provide when connecting to Hawser. A token is required
 when listening on a non-loopback address.
 .
 Leave this empty to automatically generate a token.
 The token is saved in /etc/hawser/config; use the same token when adding
 this host in Dockhand.

Template: hawser/server_url
Type: string
Description: Dockhand server WebSocket URL:
 URL of the Dockhand server to connect to in edge mode, for example
 wss://dockhand.example.com/api/hawser/connect.
 .
 Use ws:// for HTTP or wss:// for HTTPS. For a self-signed or internal CA,
 set CA_CERT in /etc/hawser/config after installation.

Template: hawser/invalid_server_url
Type: error
Description: Invalid Dockhand server URL
 The Dockhand server URL must start with ws:// or wss://.

Template: hawser/edge_token
Type: password
Description: Dockhand Edge authentication token:
 Token generated in Dockhand under Settings > Environments for a
 Hawser - Edge environment. Copy the token when Dockhand shows it.
 .
 This token is required and will not be automatically generated.

Template: hawser/missing_edge_token
Type: error
Description: Dockhand Edge token required
 Edge mode cannot connect to Dockhand without the token Dockhand generated
 for this environment.

Template: hawser/agent_name
Type: string
Description: Agent name:
 Name this agent reports to Dockhand.
 .
 Leave this empty to use the host name.
